    "steps": [
      "Slice each chicken breast horizontally into two thinner cutlets and pound to an even thickness.",
      "Set up a dredging station: flour in one dish, beaten egg in a second, and the panko mixed with the grated Parmesan in a third.",
      "Coat each cutlet in flour, then egg, then the panko-Parmesan mixture, pressing gently to help the crumbs adhere.",
      "Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and fry the cutlets for 3-4 minutes per side, until golden and cooked through; drain on a rack.",
      "Spoon a little marinara onto each cutlet, top with the mozzarella, and broil for 2-3 minutes until melted and bubbling.",
      "Meanwhile, cook the pasta in salted boiling water until al dente; toss with the remaining marinara and serve alongside the chicken."
    ],
