  {
    "id": "seed-recipe:italian-homemade-ciabatta-rolls",
    "name": "Homemade Ciabatta Rolls",
    "cuisine": "italian",
    "servings": 4,
    "sourcePresetId": null,
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "ingredientId": "seed:flour-all-purpose",
        "amountG": 300
      },
      {
        "ingredientId": "seed:water",
        "amountG": 225
      },
      {
        "ingredientId": "seed:yeast-active-dry",
        "amountG": 2,
        "sizeOptionId": "tsp"
      },
      {
        "ingredientId": "seed:salt-table",
        "amountG": 6
      },
      {
        "ingredientId": "seed:olive-oil",
        "amountG": 9
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      "In a large bowl, whisk the yeast into the water and let it sit for 5 minutes until foamy.",
      "Add the flour, salt, and olive oil. Mix with a spatula or your hands until a very wet, shaggy dough forms \u2014 it will be too sticky to knead by hand, which is normal for ciabatta's high hydration.",
      "Cover the bowl and let the dough rise at room temperature for 1.5-2 hours, until roughly doubled and full of bubbles.",
      "Generously flour a work surface and turn the dough out without deflating it too much. Divide into 4 equal pieces and gently shape each into a rough rectangle, keeping as much air in the dough as possible.",
      "Transfer the rolls to a floured or parchment-lined baking sheet, dust with flour, and let rest uncovered for 30-40 minutes while the oven preheats to 450\u00b0F (232\u00b0C).",
      "Bake for 20-25 minutes until the crust is deep golden brown and the rolls sound hollow when tapped on the bottom. Cool on a wire rack for at least 15 minutes before slicing."
    ],
